{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790978360,"nonce":"alm20lRZKhqXO5n460bkcad8TTk=","message":"Landed as `9369c824` on `worktree-agent-adf3f92dc7d1c369a`.\n\nSpace on the description tab opens the issue's first comment in a second\n`commentBox` (`showPage.desc`), focused by `editingDesc`, on the body's\ncurrent text. Enter writes it with `host.IssueCommentEdit` on that comment's\ncombined id and reloads the page; alt+enter is a newline; esc leaves the\neditor keeping the draft, which is the description's own and never the\ncomment box's. An empty body rings the bell with `a description cannot be\nemptied`, the model having no issue without a first comment. The hint on the\ntab reads `space: edit · ←→: tab`, and inside the editor\n`enter: write · alt+enter: newline · esc: leave` (`descHints`), drawn both in\nthe bottom line and in a footer under the box, the way the comment box's is.\n\nCalls made beyond the brief:\n\n- Enter's hint says **write**, not *send*: the description is one text being\n  rewritten, not one more comment.\n- The editor stands in the tab's place while it is open **and while it holds\n  an unwritten draft**, so the text being rewritten is where the text being\n  read was and a kept draft is never out of sight. Space gets back into it.\n- An editor opened and left untouched keeps nothing (`descDirty` compares the\n  draft with the stored body): an unchanged text is not a draft.\n- Leaving the page with a changed, unwritten description asks for a second\n  esc, as a comment draft already did — otherwise it would die silently.\n- Esc is the only way out of the editor; tab and the tab-switching keys are\n  text while it is open, because switching tabs would leave it behind.\n\nTests in `tui/show_test.go`: `TestSpaceOnTheDescriptionTabEditsIt` (opens on\nthe current text, an untouched esc keeps nothing, typing then enter writes —\nread back with `host.IssueGet`, `Comments[0]` — and the tab redraws from the\nstore) and `TestTheDescriptionEditorKeepsADraft` (esc keeps it, space returns\nto it, the store is untouched, an emptied body is refused). The show cases in\n`tui/hints_test.go` cover the three new hint lines.\n\nDocs: the description bullet in the Show section of\n`doc/design/terminal-renderer.md`, and AGENTS.md's show sentence.\n\n`gofmt -l`, `go vet ./tui/` and `go test ./...` pass.","files":null}]}